WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.531
When the video or the bike falls short, the class goes on, and Class Ride says so.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:14.775
When the class video cannot play, because it is blocked or the player fails, a

00:00:14.775 --> 00:00:19.510
notice appears under it. The clock, the plan and the bike carry on, and the stepper

00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:20.495
still works.

00:00:25.809 --> 00:00:30.846
With no network, YouTube's player reports no error. It only waits. So a video that

00:00:30.846 --> 00:00:35.884
has not played for ten seconds of the ride gets the same notice, and loses it when

00:00:35.884 --> 00:00:37.105
it plays again.

00:00:41.295 --> 00:00:46.069
Some bikes report but will not be controlled. Then the stepper is disabled, and a

00:00:46.069 --> 00:00:50.730
notice under the bike panel tells the rider to set the resistance by hand.

00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:02.220
The bike is asked for control once. If it says no, stays silent for three seconds,

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:07.661
or has no control point, no resistance command is ever sent, even after it is lost

00:01:07.661 --> 00:01:08.956
and comes back.

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:16.831
Both can happen at once. Each notice keeps its place, and in landscape nothing

00:01:16.831 --> 00:01:17.599
scrolls.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:25.665
The bike set by hand, from a phone to a desktop.

00:01:32.913 --> 00:01:37.960
The tests came first. Twelve failed, as expected; nine passed on the code carried

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:42.821
over. Now three hundred and thirty-six specs and one thousand four hundred and

00:01:42.821 --> 00:01:44.803
sixty-four unit tests pass.

00:01:48.399 --> 00:01:54.053
Telo Ride 1, from the Telo family, is the focused edition of Telo Ride: one class,

00:01:54.053 --> 00:01:55.249
nothing else.

00:01:55.594 --> 00:02:00.546
It pairs with a smart bike at home over Bluetooth, plays the class video, or draws

00:02:00.546 --> 00:02:05.558
the Ibiza Sunset Strip course to music if the rider chooses it, and sets the bike's

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:09.059
resistance for every interval while the rider pedals.

00:02:09.405 --> 00:02:13.380
Connect the bike, take the class, see your number, and come back to beat it.
